<title>USA: Enron Corp Q2 loss.</title>
<headline>Enron Corp Q2 loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $1.71   profit	 $0.46</p>
<p> Shr loss diluted	 $1.71   profit	 $0.43</p>
<p> Net			420,000   profit     117,000</p>
<p> Revs		   3,240,000		2,961,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 248,000		  246,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     248,000		  271,000</p>
<p>			  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.83   profit	 $1.31</p>
<p> Shr loss diluted	 $0.83   profit	 $1.22</p>
<p> Net			198,000   profit	   330</p>
<p> Revs		   8,584,000		6,015,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 248,000		  245,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     248,000		  270,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: 1997 losses include $100 million pretax charge to reflect depressed MTBE margins. This equal to $74 million after taxes, or $0.30/shr. Losses also include previously announced J-block charge of $675 million. This equal to $450 million after taxes, or $1.81/shr. Q2 per share before charges was $0.40.</p>
<p>First Call consensus was $0.39.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
